{"name":"Hōjicha","hex":"#424f3b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Hōjicha","blocks":[{"text":"Hōjicha  is a Japanese green tea. It is distinctive from other Japanese green teas because it is roasted in a porcelain pot over charcoal. It is roasted at 150 °C (302 °F) to prevent oxidation and produce a light golden colour, as opposed to other Japanese teas which are steamed. In general, the base of a hōjicha consists of leaves from the second harvest or after."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Houjicha.jpg/330px-Houjicha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H%C5%8Djicha","wikidata":"Q1652744"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Image-Hoji-cha-2.JPG/500px-Image-Hoji-cha-2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Image-Hoji-cha-2.JPG/500px-Image-Hoji-cha-2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cup of prepared hōjicha, showing the distinctive golden colour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImage-Hoji-cha-2.JPG"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_grey_mongoose_(Urva_edwardsii)_mating_2.jpg","share":0.32875},{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_g